## UI Craft: Workspace project card grid

Stack: vanilla HTML/CSS plus a small demo script · Theme: light + dark · States: complete

No `design/tokens.css` or other tokens exist, and this is a single component, so the cold-start question is skipped. I used the default `design-system` token names. When a foundation arrives, delete the token block and link `design/tokens.css`.

I did not run a browser check, so nothing here is verified at 1440px or 390px. I did not run an automated contrast check either. The colour pairs are the skill's documented defaults, not measured values. Project names and descriptions are labelled placeholders. There are no invented metrics.

### Tokens and architecture
- **Tokens:** `--color-surface-*`, `--color-text-*`, `--color-border-*`, `--color-border-focus`, `--color-danger-*`, `--color-action-primary-*`, `--glass-bg`, `--r-*` and the `--z-*` scale. Light is the default, with `[data-theme="dark"]` and `prefers-color-scheme: dark` overrides.
- **Layout:** `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(280px, 100%), 1fr))` with a 16px gap. It becomes one column at 390px with no sideways scroll.
- **Card:**
  - It is an `<article>` with one `<button aria-pressed>` as the title, stretched over the card with `::after`.
  - The footer `Open` button sits above it with `z-index`, so no button is nested inside another.
  - The skeleton and the real card share `min-height: 176px`, so there is no layout shift.
  - The primary action stays the single filled button per view (none is needed inside the grid). Card actions are secondary.

